WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.315
Northwind Logistics is a small freight company.

2
00:00:03.315 --> 00:00:05.965
It wants a bank account and a credit line.

3
00:00:05.965 --> 00:00:09.624
Both banks must know who the business is, and who owns it.

4
00:00:10.473 --> 00:00:17.683
Today that means sending the same formation documents and ownership chart to each bank, and sending them again when anything changes.

5
00:00:18.533 --> 00:00:20.716
Here, Northwind has a pod.

6
00:00:20.716 --> 00:00:22.060
It starts empty.

7
00:00:22.909 --> 00:00:27.697
A registry issues the company's identity, with its legal entity identifier.

8
00:00:27.697 --> 00:00:31.974
The identifier in this demo is illustrative, and is not a real one.

9
00:00:32.825 --> 00:00:34.836
It states who may act for the company.

10
00:00:35.686 --> 00:00:38.710
And it records the four owners and their shares.

11
00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:43.183
The full ownership table now sits in Northwind's pod, and nowhere else.

12
00:00:44.034 --> 00:00:49.901
The first bank asks to read the identity and the ownership record, for customer due diligence.

13
00:00:49.901 --> 00:00:52.210
Northwind's managing member approves.

14
00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:59.694
The bank runs the check the rule requires: every owner with a quarter or more, and the person in control.

15
00:00:59.694 --> 00:01:03.927
It reads signed data, checks each signature, and opens the account.

16
00:01:04.778 --> 00:01:07.848
The second bank is only quoting for a credit line.

17
00:01:07.848 --> 00:01:10.365
It does not need the ownership table yet.

18
00:01:10.365 --> 00:01:15.828
It needs one answer: is there any owner above a quarter that we have not been told about?

19
00:01:16.678 --> 00:01:18.619
Northwind answers with a proof.

20
00:01:18.619 --> 00:01:21.562
The bank learns the answer, and not the shares.

21
00:01:22.412 --> 00:01:26.225
Once the bank decides to lend, the rule needs the real values.

22
00:01:26.225 --> 00:01:28.316
So the proof gives way to a grant.

23
00:01:29.167 --> 00:01:30.662
One owner sells his stake.

24
00:01:30.662 --> 00:01:34.627
The registry issues a new ownership record and withdraws the old one.

25
00:01:35.477 --> 00:01:39.765
Both banks read the new record through the grants they already have.

26
00:01:39.765 --> 00:01:41.720
Nobody starts onboarding again.

27
00:01:42.571 --> 00:01:47.260
Northwind closes its account at the first bank and withdraws the grant.

28
00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:49.373
The bank's next read is refused.

29
00:01:49.373 --> 00:01:52.477
It keeps the due diligence record it must keep.

30
00:01:52.477 --> 00:01:54.326
It can no longer refresh it.

31
00:01:55.177 --> 00:02:01.524
For a supervisor, the ledger lists each due diligence obligation beside the grant and the reads that met it.

32
00:02:02.374 --> 00:02:05.748
One set of credentials, two banks, no document packs.

33
00:02:05.748 --> 00:02:12.561
If your organisation issues or relies on business identity, we would like you in the Community of Practice.
